{
    "background_story": "Thiago was a young monk who lived in the 8th century monastery of Wearmouth-Jarrow, where the Venerable Bede spent most of his life. Thiago was deeply devoted to his faith and spent most of his days studying the scriptures and assisting the monastery's scribes. He was particularly fascinated by the works of Bede, who was renowned for his knowledge of scripture, history, and science. Thiago often sought guidance from Bede, who became a mentor to him. As he delved deeper into Bede's writings, Thiago discovered a passion for history and began to assist Bede in his research. Together, they pored over ancient texts, and Thiago learned the art of historiography from the master himself. Thiago's dedication to his faith and his work with Bede led him to become a respected scholar in his own right, carrying on Bede's legacy for generations to come.",
